   "evidence": "Dyadic.lean:41-57 defines all three but bridges only `periphC`; its own proofs unfold by hand (`simp [periphC, periphP, periphT, cusp_def, List.ofFn_succ]` line 57, `simpa [periphP] using hc 0` line 77, `simpa [defect_def, periphP, periphT, List.ofFn_succ] using h` line 91). Existing basis API confirmed at Peripheral/Basic.lean:79-108. Roadmap Suggested.lean:422-432 pins the defs and `periphC_eq_cusp` but is explicitly non-exhaustive (README.md:140-141), so adding the two bridges is in scope.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/Algebra/Group/Profinite/Free/Peripheral/Dyadic.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] theorem periphP_eq_basis (e) : periphP e = basis e 0 := rfl` and `@[simp] theorem periphT_eq_basis (e) : periphT e = basis e 1 := rfl`, mirroring `periphC_eq_cusp`; then lines 57, 77, 78 and 91 no longer need `simp [periphP]`/`simp [periphT]` unfolding and the Layer 0 basis lemmas apply to `P` and `T`.",
   "issue": "`periphP e := basis e 0` (line 43) and `periphT e := basis e 1` (line 47) are wrappers with no bridging lemma back to `basis`, while `periphC` does get `@[simp] periphC_eq_cusp` (line 56). Consumers of `P`/`T` therefore cannot apply the existing basis theory (`basis_apply`, `map_basis`, `hom_ext_basis`, `topologicalClosure_closure_range_basis` in Peripheral/Basic.lean:82-108) without unfolding a definition, and simp normal forms are mixed: after simp a goal in all three elements becomes `periphP e * periphT e * cusp (basis e)`.",
   "line": "43"
  }
